  "dom_id": "question-142976",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "The amount of hemoglobin in the bloodstream of people living in a particular Colorado community follows a normal distribution. An analysis on a random sample of $16$ people yields a mean hemoglobin concentration of $13.1\\,\\text{g/dl}$ with a sample standard deviation of $1.8\\,\\text{g/dl}.$ Find a $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean hemoglobin concentration $\\mu $ for all people in the community.  \n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores ${t}_{k,p}$ such that $P(T>{t}_{k,p})=p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p.$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $15$ | $1.341$ | $1.753$ | $2.131$ | $2.602$ | $2.947$ |\n| $16$ | $1.337$ | $1.746$ | $2.120$ | $2.583$ | $2.921$ |\n| $17$ | $1.333$ | $1.740$ | $2.110$ | $2.576$ | $2.898$ |",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
